We use [ransack](https://activerecord-hackery.github.io/ransack/) to add filters and
sorting to a list. Also, for pagination, we use the [pagy](https://ddnexus.github.io/pagy/) gem.

Here's an example:

```rb
# users_controller.rb

def index
  @query = User.ransack(params[:q])
  @pagy, @users = pagy(@query.result, limit: 3)
end
```

```erb
<%%# users/index.html.erb %>

<%%= card_component(padding: false) do |card| %>
  <%% card.with_header do %>
    <div class="flex justify-between items-center">
      <h3 class="text-lg leading-6 font-medium text-gray-900">Users</h3>

      <%%= search_form_for @query, data: { controller: 'search-form' } do |f| %>
        <%%= search_field_component(form: f, name: :email_or_first_name_or_last_name_cont) %>
      <%% end %>
    </div>
  <%% end %>

  <div class="border-t border-gray-200">
    <%%= table_component do |table| %>
      <thead>
        <%% table.with_header(align: :left) do %>
          <%%= sort_link(@query, :email) %>
        <%% end %>
        <%% table.with_header do %>
          <%%= sort_link(@query, :first_name) %>
        <%% end %>
        <%% table.with_header do %>
          <%%= sort_link(@query, :last_name) %>
        <%% end %>
      </thead>

      <tbody>
        <%%= render @users %>
      </tbody>
    <%% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="border-t border-gray-200">
    <%%= pagination_component(pagy: @pagy) %>
  </div>
<%% end %>
```

Check the [pagination](<%= lookbook_inspect_path('navigation/pagination/default') %>)
and [search field](<%= lookbook_inspect_path('form/search_field/default') %>) components.

